  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Coordination Guard Availability Audit",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Scope",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Audit target: why governed edit tools are being blocked by the coordination guard and whether the cause is real active protection, stale leases, overly broad reservations, missing expiry, broken path normalization, or a tool integration bug.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This audit is read-only. It does not delete leases, bypass the guard, or mutate `/Users/user/.rig/relay`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Git State",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Branch: `main` - HEAD: `384e486` - Dirty status: pre-existing dirty files were already present before this audit; they were not modified by this audit.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Coordination Guard Layout",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Lease and coordination state live under:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `.build/rig-relay/coordination/sessions/` - `.build/rig-relay/coordination/tasks/` - `.build/rig-relay/coordination/leases/paths/` - `.build/rig-relay/coordination/events.jsonl`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The authoritative store is `rig_relay/coordination/store.py`. Lease cleanup logic exists in `rig_relay/coordination/cleanup_leases.py`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Guard Mechanics Observed",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Dirty-file protection",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`rig_relay/governance/dirty_guard.py` captures the repo dirty set at mission start using `git status --porcelain=v1` and blocks writes to paths that were already dirty unless the caller supplies an expected hash for the protected file.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This is correct active protection for pre-existing dirty files.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-15",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Coordination reservations",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`rig_relay/coordination/store.py` stores path reservations in `.build/rig-relay/coordination/leases/paths/*.json` and claims in `.build/rig-relay/coordination/tasks/*.json`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`search_replace` and `write_file` both claim coordination and reserve write paths before mutating. When reservation fails, they raise `ToolError(\"... coordination reservation refused\")`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Inventory Summary",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Read-only inventory of the coordination store on this repo snapshot:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Lease/task records scanned: `512` - Active records: `318` - Released records: `193` - Stale records: `1` - Unique active path targets: `94` - Unique active paths that overlap current git-dirty files: `52`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The overlap with git-dirty files indicates that a large share of the blocking is real protection of existing user-owned or prior-agent-owned changes.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-22",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Blocked Tool Names",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The blocked governed mutation surfaces observed in this audit are:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `search_replace` - `write_file` - coordination-aware write/checkpoint flows that consult the same reservation store",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "These tools are blocked when the coordination store refuses a reservation or when the dirty guard marks the target as protected.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-26",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Blocked Paths",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The most frequent blocked paths are concentrated in the current mutation backlog:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `vibe/core/tools/builtins/search_replace.py` - `vibe/core/tools/builtins/validate.py` - `tests/tools/test_validate.py` - `rig_relay/evidence/model_observations.py` - `scripts/rig_relay_contribute_telemetry_bundle.py` - `rig_relay/evidence/receipt_index.py` - `tests/evidence/test_receipt_index.py` - `docs/governance/telemetry-contribution-policy.md` - `tests/test_observation_consent_integration.py` - `tests/tools/test_tool_receipt_emission.py` - `tests/tools/test_hardened_tools.py` - `tests/tools/test_bash_hardening.py` - `tests/test_model_observations.py` - `vibe/core/telemetry/constants.py` - `vibe/core/tools/builtins/bash.py`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "There is also a clean-path reservation example:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `docs/audits/rig-intake-cannibalization-plan.md`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "That means the guard is not only protecting dirty files; it is also carrying forward explicit coordination reservations from active or recent missions.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-32",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Active vs Stale Classification",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-33",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Active protection",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Most blocked paths are explained by active coordination records plus pre-existing dirty files. This is expected behavior.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-35",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Stale lease",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "At least one stale lease was present:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Lease file: `.build/rig-relay/coordination/leases/paths/cbb9f7f7b6feca9630da295cd47372af998cf2d615f355c14e68cc5730e5fd90.json` - Session: `session_20260513_220723_3b1ecec2` - Task: `call_00_0BqXT2mIh4vx09Leo1b69752` - Path: `/Users/user/Developer/GitHub/rig-relay/tests/scripts/test_desktop_projection.py` - Expiry: `2026-05-13T22:13:03.918976+00:00`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This is a stale lease candidate, not evidence of a current live owner.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-39",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Broad scope risk",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The reservation set is broader than the current mutation slice in a few places. The same mission family has reservations spanning many unrelated files, so a tool may be blocked even when the caller is trying to edit a different file in the same repo.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This suggests the guard is sometimes enforcing a valid lease at too coarse a scope rather than failing open.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-42",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Path normalization risk",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`rig_relay/coordination/store.py` normalizes paths for payloads, but some lookup and conflict checks mix raw input paths and normalized paths. Reservation files are keyed by a composite hash, while conflict lookup also hashes raw paths for existence checks.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-44",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "That is a plausible source of false conflicts or stale-release friction, especially for equivalent but differently-formatted paths.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-45",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Root Cause Assessment",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-46",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Correct active protection",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Yes, for most of the observed blocking.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Evidence:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- 52 unique active paths overlap current git-dirty files. - The repo has a large pre-existing dirty set. - The coordination store contains many active reservations tied to current mission files.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-50",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Stale lease",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Present, but not the primary blocker.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-52",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Evidence:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-53",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- At least one expired reservation still exists as a stale record.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-54",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Overly broad lease scope",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-55",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Likely contributing factor.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Evidence:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-57",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Active reservations span 94 unique paths while current mutations are concentrated in a smaller set of files. - Some reserved paths are in audit/docs or adjacent tool files rather than the exact target slice.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-58",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Missing lease expiry",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Not the main issue.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-60",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Evidence:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-61",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Expiry fields are present on the records. - The issue is more about cleanup and scope than absence of expiry metadata.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-62",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Broken path normalization",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Plausible and worth fixing.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-64",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Evidence:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-65",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `store.py` compares raw and normalized paths in different places. - Reservation file identity and lookup are not using a single obvious canonical key path throughout the code.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-66",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Tool integration bug",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-67",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Yes.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-68",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Evidence:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-69",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `search_replace` and `write_file` convert reservation refusal into `ToolError` instead of a structured result envelope. - That makes blocked outcomes harder to reason about and easier for agents to work around with raw bash.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-70",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Minimal Fix Recommendation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-71",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Keep the guard enabled. 2. Narrow reservation scope where possible so unrelated edits do not inherit broad blocks. 3. ~~Make reservation refusal return a structured blocked result instead of a generic `ToolError` for governed edit tools~~ **COMPLETED** — see Structured Blocking Implementation below. 4. Normalize path identity through one canonical function for reservation write, conflict lookup, release, and expiry processing. 5. Add a focused regression test for stale lease discovery and for a clean path that is incorrectly blocked.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-72",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Structured Blocking Implementation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-73",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The third recommendation from the audit — returning structured `blocked`/`refused` results instead of generic `ToolError` — has been implemented for both `write_file` and `search_replace`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-74",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Changes to `write_file`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-75",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**File**: `vibe/core/tools/builtins/write_file.py`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-76",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **`WriteFileResult`** gained three new fields: - `status: str = \"success\"` — `\"success\"`, `\"blocked\"` (coordination), or `\"refused\"` (dirty guard) - `error_kind: str | None = None` — `\"path_reserved\"`, `\"dirty_file_protected\"`, `\"expected_hash_mismatch\"`, `\"protected_file_missing\"` - `refusal_reason: str | None = None` — human-readable detail from the guard",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-77",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. **`_classify_write_guard_refusal(check)`** — classifies `WriteGuardResult.reason` into a structured `error_kind`: - `stale_hash` / `hash_mismatch` → `\"expected_hash_mismatch\"` - `no_overwrite_flag` / `missing_expected_hash` → `\"dirty_file_protected\"` - `protected_file_missing` → `\"protected_file_missing\"` - fallback → `\"dirty_file_protected\"`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-78",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "3. **Coordination reservation failure** (`_maybe_claim_coordination()`): now returns `False` instead of `raise ToolError(...)`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-79",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "4. **`run()` coordination failure**: yields `WriteFileResult(status=\"blocked\", error_kind=\"path_reserved\", ...)` when coordination store is available but reservation is refused.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-80",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "5. **`run()` guard failure**: yields `WriteFileResult(status=\"refused\", error_kind=<classified>, refusal_reason=check.detail, ...)` instead of `raise ToolError(...)`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-81",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Changes to `search_replace`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-82",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**File**: `vibe/core/tools/builtins/search_replace.py`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-83",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **Coordination reservation failure** (`_claim_coordination()`): now returns `False` instead of `raise ToolError(...)`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-84",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. **`run()` coordination failure**: yields `SearchReplaceResult(status=\"blocked\", error_kind=\"path_reserved\", ...)` when coordination store is available but reservation is refused.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-85",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Error Kind Taxonomy",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-86",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "`error_kind`",
        "When emitted"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`path_reserved`",
          "Coordination reservation refused — path has an active lease from another session"
        ],
        [
          "`dirty_file_protected`",
          "Dirty guard blocks write because `allow_overwrite_protected=True` was not set or `expected_before_sha256` was not provided"
        ],
        [
          "`expected_hash_mismatch`",
          "`expected_before_sha256` does not match current file bytes"
        ],
        [
          "`protected_file_missing`",
          "File that was dirty at mission start no longer exists"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-87",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Design Decisions",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-88",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **Conditional blocking**: Coordination failures only yield blocked results when the coordination store is available. If the store is absent (e.g., legacy tests), `_claim_coordination()` returns `False` and `run()` proceeds normally. This preserves backward compatibility.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-89",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. **No path normalization change**: `normalize_path` in coordination models still only calls `as_posix()` without `resolve()`. Equivalent relative/absolute paths will not match. This was deferred to a follow-up.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-90",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "3. **Content-light refusals**: Both `WriteFileResult` and `SearchReplaceResult` set `content=\"\"` (and `after_sha256=\"\"`) on blocked/refused results. No raw file contents, diffs, search text, or replace text leaked into refusal metadata.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-91",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Tests Added",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-92",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "All in `tests/tools/test_hardened_tools.py`:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-93",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Test",
        "Verifies"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`test_write_file_blocked_by_active_lease_returns_structured`",
          "Coordination lease blocks → `status=\"blocked\"`, `error_kind=\"path_reserved\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`test_write_file_blocked_by_dirty_guard_returns_structured`",
          "Dirty guard blocks → `status=\"refused\"`, `error_kind=\"dirty_file_protected\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`test_write_file_hash_mismatch_returns_structured`",
          "Stale hash → `status=\"refused\"`, `error_kind=\"expected_hash_mismatch\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`test_write_file_correct_hash_succeeds`",
          "Correct hash → `status=\"success\"`, bytes written"
        ],
        [
          "`test_write_file_refusal_is_content_light`",
          "No raw file contents in refusal dump"
        ],
        [
          "`test_search_replace_blocked_by_active_lease_returns_structured`",
          "Coordination lease blocks → `status=\"blocked\"`, `error_kind=\"path_reserved\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`test_search_replace_refusal_is_content_light`",
          "No raw search/replace text in refusal dump"
        ],
        [
          "`test_path_normalization_equivalent_forms`",
          "`normalize_path` does NOT resolve — documents limitation"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-94",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Coordination-blocking tests use direct `CoordinationStore` reservations (not WriteFile-based setup) to avoid the WriteFile `finally` block releasing the lease prematurely.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-95",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Validation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-96",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- **Tests**: 67/67 pass (29 in `test_hardened_tools.py`, 20 in `test_dirty_file.py`, 18 in `test_store.py`) - **Lint**: `ruff check` clean, `ruff format` clean - **Types**: `pyright` clean (0 errors, 0 warnings on changed files) - **Schemas**: 78/78 schema validations pass",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-97",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Remaining Issues (deferred)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-98",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **Path normalization**: `normalize_path` needs `.resolve()` to match equivalent relative/absolute paths. 2. **Stale lease cleanup**: At least one stale lease remains in the coordination store. 3. **Broad lease scope**: Reservations spanning 94 unique paths create false positives.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-99",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Safe Stale-Lease Cleanup Command",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-100",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Yes, a safe cleanup command is useful, but it should remain archive-first and dry-run-first.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-101",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Recommended safe sequence:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-102",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Run the coordination lease cleanup script in dry-run mode. 2. If the result is clearly stale/released, archive first rather than delete. 3. Only consider deletion after inspecting the archive and confirming there is no live ownership.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-103",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The existing cleanup module already supports archive mode and destructive removal, so the safe operational answer is to prefer archive mode and keep deletion out of this audit mission.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-104",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Validation",
      "disclosure": {
